1
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:04,148
[Apocalypse Log 4]

2
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,841
We were just strangers who met by chance.

3
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:16,216
Oh, forget it.

4
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:30,816
Lin Zai, you're awake.

5
00:01:30,816 --> 00:01:32,357
I'll go heat up some food for you.

6
00:01:32,357 --> 00:01:33,667
No need, Grandma.

7
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,842
I'll just have some biscuits.

8
00:01:40,357 --> 00:01:41,524
- Chen.
- Yeah?

9
00:01:41,524 --> 00:01:42,857
Where's Lie?

10
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:44,774
He's gone.

11
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:46,167
He's gone?

12
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:48,300
Why didn't you tell me?

13
00:01:49,149 --> 00:01:52,157
Why tell you? Were you going to leave with him?

14
00:01:56,691 --> 00:02:00,816
In this apocalypse, it's not easy
to find a reliable companion.

15
00:02:01,941 --> 00:02:04,191
If he wasn't in such a hurry to leave,

16
00:02:04,191 --> 00:02:06,407
it would have been great if he could stay.

17
00:02:28,316 --> 00:02:30,732
Lin Zai, where are you going?

18
00:02:30,732 --> 00:02:32,824
I'm going to bring Lie back.

19
00:02:52,482 --> 00:02:53,816
Your wound hasn't healed yet.

20
00:02:53,816 --> 00:02:56,066
Why are you running around?

21
00:02:56,066 --> 00:02:57,699
You didn't leave?

22
00:02:59,107 --> 00:03:00,691
What happened to you two?

23
00:03:00,691 --> 00:03:02,107
Just bad luck.

24
00:03:02,107 --> 00:03:04,399
We fell down a slope while gathering wood.

25
00:03:04,399 --> 00:03:06,000
Luckily, it was a small one.

26
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,592
Otherwise, I'm not sure we would've
made it back today.

27
00:03:10,548 --> 00:03:11,550
Oh, man.

28
00:03:11,550 --> 00:03:12,882
My mouth is full of dirt.

29
00:03:12,882 --> 00:03:15,348
Let's chat later. I need to go wash up.

30
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,093
Hey, what are you doing?

31
00:03:31,093 --> 00:03:32,679
Put me down.

32
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:34,354
Put me down!

33
00:03:42,798 --> 00:03:45,632
Hey, what's up with you two?

34
00:03:45,632 --> 00:03:47,390
His wound opened up again.

35
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:49,923
How did that happen?

36
00:03:49,923 --> 00:03:52,215
They just went to gather wood.

37
00:03:52,215 --> 00:03:54,723
Why should an injured person tag along?

38
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:58,107
I thought...

39
00:04:03,390 --> 00:04:04,807
I... I'm fine now.

40
00:04:04,807 --> 00:04:06,307
It doesn't even hurt.

41
00:04:06,307 --> 00:04:08,057
Hey, Lin Zai.

42
00:04:08,057 --> 00:04:10,147
Wasn't your foot badly injured
a couple of days ago?

43
00:04:10,147 --> 00:04:12,077
It's almost healed now.

44
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:18,991
Don't move.

45
00:04:24,274 --> 00:04:25,699
Oh.

46
00:04:26,691 --> 00:04:29,038
Maybe it just looked scary at the time.

47
00:04:32,274 --> 00:04:33,482
Yeah.

48
00:04:33,482 --> 00:04:36,282
It's good to be young. You're resilient.

49
00:04:43,691 --> 00:04:45,232
Lie.

50
00:04:45,232 --> 00:04:47,282
You should wash up, too.

51
00:04:49,024 --> 00:04:50,616
I'll go right now.

52
00:05:00,524 --> 00:05:02,699
Don't run about.

53
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:27,008
<i>Immune target confirmed.</i>

54
00:05:49,373 --> 00:05:51,089
Laundry detergent.

55
00:05:57,875 --> 00:05:59,689
The stains on your clothes...

56
00:05:59,689 --> 00:06:02,328
Wash off as much as you can.

57
00:06:02,328 --> 00:06:03,583
No need.

58
00:06:03,583 --> 00:06:05,300
I've already dried them.

59
00:06:08,392 --> 00:06:10,025
All right then.

60
00:06:13,684 --> 00:06:16,475
You never seem to get any proper rest.

61
00:06:16,475 --> 00:06:17,809
You're always so vigilant.

62
00:06:17,809 --> 00:06:19,391
Aren't you tired?

63
00:06:20,372 --> 00:06:22,172
I'm used to it.

64
00:06:26,392 --> 00:06:27,684
Lie.

65
00:06:27,684 --> 00:06:29,900
What did you work as before all this?

66
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:34,067
I have nothing to say about the past.

67
00:06:36,517 --> 00:06:39,225
You said you still had important things to do.

68
00:06:39,225 --> 00:06:40,859
What's that about?

69
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:45,234
That's not for you to ask.

70
00:06:51,517 --> 00:06:54,600
I thought we were already friends.

71
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,900
I just wanted to know you better.

72
00:07:12,392 --> 00:07:13,683
I'm going to catch a couple of fish.

73
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,483
We'll have an extra dish tonight.

74
00:08:03,934 --> 00:08:05,359
Give me your hand.

75
00:08:11,517 --> 00:08:13,192
A gift for you.

76
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,827
Lie.

77
00:08:45,607 --> 00:08:48,149
The apocalypse has taken a lot from me.

78
00:08:48,149 --> 00:08:49,982
So, I want to cherish the people I meet,

79
00:08:49,982 --> 00:08:52,241
people I can rely on.

80
00:08:53,566 --> 00:08:56,532
I think you're very trustworthy.

81
00:09:00,774 --> 00:09:04,449
I think we could become
companions who are like family.

82
00:09:06,774 --> 00:09:10,032
I don't know what it is
that you're risking your life for.

83
00:09:10,691 --> 00:09:12,824
Maybe we can help you.

84
00:09:14,191 --> 00:09:18,607
That way, you won't have to struggle alone,

85
00:09:18,607 --> 00:09:20,574
or get hurt so much.

86
00:09:38,316 --> 00:09:41,866
So... won't you stay?

87
00:09:54,107 --> 00:09:56,125
No one can help me.

88
00:09:56,125 --> 00:09:58,054
I won't be staying.

89
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:05,041
I understand.

90
00:10:05,041 --> 00:10:06,966
When do you plan to leave?

91
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,091
Once your foot is healed, I'll leave.

92
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:19,625
Actually, you don't need to worry about me.

93
00:10:19,625 --> 00:10:21,700
I'm almost fully recovered.

94
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:22,750
Look.

95
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:24,884
I'm not even using the crutch anymore.

96
00:10:27,917 --> 00:10:29,634
Then I'll leave tomorrow.

97
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:02,250
Are you really not staying?

98
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:03,925
You've made up your mind?

99
00:11:12,458 --> 00:11:14,291
Those meant to stay will stay,

100
00:11:14,291 --> 00:11:17,791
and those who want to leave
cannot be forced to stay.

101
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:20,383
It's enough that we met.

102
00:11:25,791 --> 00:11:30,175
All good things must come to an end.

103
00:11:30,175 --> 00:11:31,758
Lie.

104
00:11:31,758 --> 00:11:36,197
Wherever you go,
take good care of yourself, okay?

105
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:38,433
Thank you.

106
00:11:40,217 --> 00:11:42,092
Buddy.

107
00:11:42,092 --> 00:11:44,842
I really don't want you to go.

108
00:11:44,842 --> 00:11:49,758
If you stay here, we'll feel so much safer.

109
00:11:49,758 --> 00:11:52,717
Since you've already decided,

110
00:11:52,717 --> 00:11:55,100
I won't say anything more.

111
00:11:58,842 --> 00:12:00,550
We're parting ways tomorrow.

112
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:04,967
Let's treat this meal
as a farewell party for Lie.

113
00:12:04,967 --> 00:12:07,550
Let's drink until we drop tonight.

114
00:12:07,550 --> 00:12:09,592
Come on, bro.

115
00:12:09,592 --> 00:12:10,975
Fill it up.

116
00:12:16,175 --> 00:12:17,683
Come on.

117
00:12:18,842 --> 00:12:20,217
Your foot hasn't healed yet.

118
00:12:20,217 --> 00:12:21,717
You shouldn't drink.

119
00:12:21,717 --> 00:12:22,708
It's fine.

120
00:12:22,708 --> 00:12:24,758
Didn't you see my injury today?

121
00:12:24,758 --> 00:12:26,392
Besides...

122
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:28,258
Since we've met,

123
00:12:28,258 --> 00:12:30,417
I have to have a drink.

124
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:32,800
Since you've put it that way...

125
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,558
Fill it up.

126
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,884
Come on.

127
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:43,717
I hope we'll meet again one day.

128
00:12:45,508 --> 00:12:50,517
I hope every one of you stays safe and well.

129
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:56,633
I hope the zombie crisis ends soon.

130
00:12:59,042 --> 00:13:00,884
I hope...

131
00:13:02,383 --> 00:13:04,850
I hope everyone's wishes come true.

132
00:13:14,125 --> 00:13:15,967
Cheers.

133
00:14:20,175 --> 00:14:21,642
Lie.

134
00:14:22,383 --> 00:14:24,925
<i>The apocalypse has taken a lot from me.</i>

135
00:14:24,925 --> 00:14:26,758
<i>So, I want to cherish the people I meet,</i>

136
00:14:26,758 --> 00:14:29,017
<i>the people I can rely on.</i>

137
00:14:30,342 --> 00:14:33,308
<i>I think you're very trustworthy.</i>

138
00:14:37,125 --> 00:14:40,704
<i>So... won't you stay?</i>

